# Secure mode service posture — one unit per line, '+' to ensure-started,
# '-' to ensure-stopped. Read by raptor_mode_managerd._apply_services().
# NOTE: nftables must NOT be toggled here — its ExecStart/ExecStop both
# `nft flush ruleset`, which would wipe the {mode}.nft table loaded just
# before this step. The firewall is owned by _apply_firewall() only.
#
# Secure is this OS's privacy baseline, so Tor and its DNS resolver run here
# too (dnsmasq forwards 127.0.0.1:53 -> Tor DNSPort 9053; Mode Manager points
# resolv.conf at 127.0.0.1 once these are up, so queries never touch the
# clearnet).
+ NetworkManager
+ tor@default
+ dnsmasq